// TEST: Three-argument comm claim disproved by a witness (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4013
// ERROR-CONTAINS: (with z = 0.75)
// `comm(x, y, z)` claims invariance under every permutation of the three
// slots, and `x + 2.0 * y + 3.0 * z` has none of it. The witness evaluator
// used to give up on any parameter beyond the swapped pair, so a false claim
// on a kernel of arity > 2 was never refused: it was stored on the simplex
// i <= j <= k and every other ordering read back a value the body never
// produced. The other parameters are now held at fixed values across the
// swap, and the counterexample names them.
let A = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let R = method_for(A, A, A) <@> lambda(x, y, z) where comm(x, y, z) -> x + 2.0 * y + 3.0 * z |> compute
